WEBVTT

﻿1

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.124
[car engines humming]


00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.810
[distant laughter]


00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.969
- When I saw Claire again
for the first time that summer,


00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.287
it was at a party given by-


00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.200
oh, let's say the Xs
near the Place de Ia Concorde.


00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.322
The entire summer
had been lovely,


00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.968
but that evening
was particularly beautiful.


00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.129
I was late, as usual.


00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.288
Normally, I detest literary
cocktail parties...


00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.890
- Jean!
- Hi.


00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.923
As anyone who attends them
regularly should,


00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.407
if he has any self-respect
at all.


00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.726
- [laughs]


00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.763
- I had just come out
of a long siege


00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.291
with a short story,


00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.562
a short story that had
an enormous resistance


00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.806
to being completed,


00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.002
and, had Ito be
totally honest,


00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.527
I would confess that I was
genuinely pleased


00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.051
to be once more
among the living.


00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:28.764
Ah, how are you?


00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:29.767
- And you?
- Fine.


00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.360
- Good.


00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.925
Excuse me.


00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.566
What struck me most
about seeing Claire again


00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.331
was that she hadn't
changed at all.


00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.920
I felt as if I had just
left her the night before.


00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.088
Although, in reality,
I hadn't seen her


00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.204
for at least two
or three years, maybe more.


00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.330
- Friedlander?


00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.322
- Coudrain.


00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.050
- I said hello to other people,


00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.401
but I meticulously avoided
getting involved


00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.648
in the peculiar
kind of pointless argument


00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.127
which is so typical
at that kind of party.


00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.204
I remember that I noticed
something then


00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.164
in which I wouldn't have minded
getting involved,


00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.681
and it was dressed
all in white.


00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.444
As I think back, she had made
more of an impression on me


00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.245
than the usual pretty girl
one sees at parties.


00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.887
The young girl
in the white dress and Claire


00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.048
were friends,
obviously.


00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:31.290
But beyond that, I sensed
a strange link between them,


00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.925
a kind of electricity,


00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.690
although I had never
heard it said


00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.009
that Claire was particularly
interested in girls.


00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.044
Still, there was a conspiracy
between them


00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.846
that one could
feel quite clearly.


00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.724
:Tl


00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.647
- What are you doing
hiding out there?


00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.922
- Oh, thinking
of clever things to say


00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.042
to your delightful guests.


00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.050
- That shouldn't be
too difficult for you.


00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.844
- What about the young girl
in the white dress?


00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.086
- I don't know a thing
about her.


00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.242
She came with Claire.


00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.169
I suppose she's a friend
of hers.


00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.930
Funny thing is,
I haven't been able


00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.969
to get two words out of her
all night.


00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.970
- I remembered clearly
the look Claire had given her.


00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.527
It was the look of one viewing
a rerun of a successful film


00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.290
one had directed oneself,


00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.529
whose plot couldn't possibly
have any surprises.


00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.567
- Lovely to have had you.


00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.205
- Later, as I was getting
ready to leave...


00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.401
- Jean.
- All right,


00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.686
I might call you later.
- Jean.


00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.131
- Yes?


00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:57.844
- If you like, perhaps
we could have a drink somewhere


00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.200
to forget about
this dreadful party.


00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.691
- Nice.


00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.450
- You can get to know Anne.


00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:03.686
- Anne?


00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.245
- Anne.


00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.486
You'll see.


00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.568
She's very nice.


00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.170
- Who is she, anyway?


00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.046
- Oh, just a young model.


00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.286
- And?


00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.404
- Well, she belongs to me.


00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.570
[dog growling and barking]


00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.570
[soft music playing]


00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.641
Three mineral waters, please.


00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:56.204
She's pretty, isn't she?


00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.207
- Yes, very.


00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.207
- She's very pretty.


00:05:58.320 --> 00:05:59.651
You can touch her if you like.


00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.561
And she has a beautiful mouth,


00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:08.605
lovely soft lips,


00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.764
lovely, soft, knowing lips.


00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.291
And pretty teeth.


00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.525
Come, let's have a look at them.


00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:25.244
Stay like that.


00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.483
Someday I'll show you
some photographs I took of her.


00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:42.801
- Claire had arranged to meet me
the following day.


00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.009
I knew enough by now not to ask
whether we would be alone


00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.043
or with her young friend.


00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.401
We were supposed to spend
the afternoon together


00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.760
in the Bagatelle Gardens,


00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:55.282
the most beautiful rose garden
in the world.


00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.731
She had insisted
that she wanted


00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.285
to show it to me herself.


00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.925
Claire was a stunning woman


00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.646
and probably even more
interesting than her friend.


00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:07.163
But unlike her friend, she had
never aroused me at all.


00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.322
At first this had bothered me.


00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.683
But then I told myself that it
was her impeccable manners


00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.007
and the precise way
in which she did everything


00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.491
that made it impossible


00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.001
to think about her
as a potential conquest.


00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.203
I probably needed to feel
that at least some little thing


00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.129
was vulnerable in order
to arouse


00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:25.685
a desire in me to win her.


00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.800
Claire was waiting for us
in the car.


00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.365
Anne's manner reminded me


00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.290
of a well-behaved
young schoolgirl.


00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.290
I had time to ask the girl
several casual questions,


00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.324
but all I could get out of her
was, "Yes, monsieur,"


00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.211
"No, monsieur," or,
"I don't know, monsieur,"


00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.129
as though she were a child.


00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.284
[tires screech]


00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.164
Instead of letting us wander
from flower to flower,


00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:18.964
Claire made us look
at the varieties


00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.445
that she admired most,


00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.490
knowing exactly
where each one was.


00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.490
[bright instrumental music]


00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.884
After the grand tour,
we wandered off


00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.241
toward a more deserted part
of the garden.


00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:29.967
- Go over to it.


00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:33.368
Go on.
Hurry up.


00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:42.090
Now go ahead.


00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.406
Watch this.


00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.329
She has pretty hands.


00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.044
- Yes.


00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.242
- She likes doing that,
you know.


00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:00.521
It excites her.


00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:04.247
I can prove it to you,
if you like.


00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:06.601
At the slightest provocation,
she gets all wet.


00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.768
Isn't that right, little one?


00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.250
All right, that's enough.


00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:30.207
Pick the flower
and bring it over here.


00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.243
Well, what are you waiting for?


00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.481
- Ifs not allowed.


00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.409
- Nothing that I like
is allowed, Anne.


00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:36.487
You know that.


00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:37.601
- There are too many thorns.


00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.882
- You simply have
to get scratched.


00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:47.562
Very good.


00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.728
And it wasn't too difficult,
was it?


00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.410
Of course, you will be punished


00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:54.490
for having hesitated
just a second too long.


00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:56.045
- What are you planning to do?


00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:57.207
- I don't know.


00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.845
But she'll be punished
in front of you.


00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.962
- Somebody's coming.


00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:03.128
- All right, bring the flower.


00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:06.601
- Excuse me.


00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.767
What time is it, please?


00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:09.803
- 10:30.


00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:12.161
- We continued our walk.


00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:13.566
Anne, in the middle,


00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:15.205
held the rose
against her breast


00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.886
so no one could detect
her crime.


00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:21.322
We soon came
to a sort of grove or thicket,


00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:24.011
more or less closed off
from the rest of the gardens


00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.571
and completely deserted.


00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.569
Since there weren't
any flowers,


00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:31.127
we reasoned that here
we could find some privacy.


00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:34.562
- This will be all right.


00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:35.727


00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.120
She'll have to stand.


00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:39.891
She has to think about
where to hide what she's stolen.


00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:40.887
The rose must be hidden.


00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.367
- All she has to do
is throw it over there.


00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:46.529
- But it would be such a shame
to lose such a beautiful flower.


00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.489
- Yes.


00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.688


00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:51.687
I don't know.


00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:53.245
- Ifs very simple.


00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.647
You'll have to hide it
somewhere on your person.


00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:56.761
Come over here.


00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.405
Lift your skirt.


00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:05.369
Lift your skirt.


00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:06.720
You'll have to lift it
higher than that.


00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.446
Hurry up.


00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:13.360
Higher.


00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.322
Well, what do you think of it?


00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:21.044
- The design on the tops
of the stockings


00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.527
is a particularly charming
touch.


00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:28.160
- [gasps]


00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.328
- What we will do
is slip the stem


00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:32.329
up between the garter belt


00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.767
and the skin about there
close to the crotch.


00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.211
The thorns should
be strong enough


00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:38.607
to hold the flower in place.


00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:40.210
- Only when she's
standing still.


00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.931
- See how nice I am?


00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:46.169
I'm taking off
all the little thorns


00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.806
so as not to hurt you.


00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:50.445
Oh, but I forgot.


00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:53.803
She's supposed to be punished,
isn't she?


00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:58.087
Spread your legs apart,
and then don't move.


00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.646
I'm going to hurt you.


00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.802
Come close to me.


00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:06.251
- Please, please don't.


00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.885
I beg you.


00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.126
Please.


00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:10.366


00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:11.720
- Now hold still.


00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:14.207
- Oh, no, please.


00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.486
Please, no.


00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.728
No, no.


00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.649
[shouts]


00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:23.764
[gasping]


00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:45.841
- There.


00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.042
That's pretty, isn't it?


00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.889
- A great success,


00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.889
but perhaps rather overburdened
with symbols in,


00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:55.004
I would say,
the surrealist tradition.


00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:02.244
[birds chirping]


00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:58.443
- You may lower your dress.


00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:01.564
[birds chirping]


00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:14.804
Can you still feel the petals
between your thighs?


00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:16.604
Does it feel nice?


00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.007
Well, can't you answer?


00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:20.804
- Yes, it feels nice.


00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:22.365
I have-


00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:23.646
I need to stop a minute.


00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:24.761
- No, you can't go now.


00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.611
You didn't have to drink so much
water in the first place.


00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:31.930
- I didn't know yet what Claire
was leading us up to.


00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:39.409
At last, we came to an area


00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:41.841
that seemed more wild
and natural,


00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.049
where very large trees
had blanketed the sparse,


00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:47.322
unkempt grass
with fallen leaves.


00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:48.566
- This is the perfect place.


00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:49.806
Don't you think so?


00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.331
- Depends on what you want
to use it for.


00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.601
- For the little girl,
of course.


00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:53.841
She was looking for a bathroom.


00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.611
- Oh, no, I don't need to go.


00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.165
- Why did you lie to us?


00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:00.362
I thought you were going
to give us a little performance.


00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:02.727
- No, I was mistaken.


00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.444
- Don't try to fool with us.


00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:08.326
You know it won't
get you anywhere, Anne.


00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:11.011
Anne.


00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:14.726
You'll do it now.


00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.765
Bend down lower.


00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:36.961
Now, then.


00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.765
Ls our little girl
going to do pee-pee?


00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:45.960
Be sure your legs are spread
far enough apart.


00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:50.242
That's fine.


00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.970
Now lean forward a little.


00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:02.167
You're very nice like that,
you know?


00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:10.246
Well, are you going to piss
or not, you little bitch?


00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:16.962
- [gasps]


00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:22.004
[whimpers]


00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:19.684
[engine roaring]


00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.206
- More than a week went by


00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:40.881
without my seeing Claire
or Anne again.


00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.729
On the eighth day,
quite by chance,


00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.683
I was driving
on the Quai Malaquais


00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:47.690
and I ran into little Anne
at the book stalls.


00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:50.804
She was alone,
and that pleased me.


00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:13.047
She pretended
not to recognize me,


00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:15.447
which hardly surprised me,
I must say.


00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:21.088
I thought of that
last image I had


00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:24.409
of our afternoon
in the Bagatelle Gardens.


00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:26.682
The girl was now speaking
to the salesman.


00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:30.009
- No, we haven't got any more.


00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:32.043
- Look, I know you have
what I want.


00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:33.730
I'm going to stand here
till I get it.


00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:35.046
- I don't handle
that type of book.


00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:36.571
- All right,
I can find it myself.


00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:38.170
- I was struck by the positive
tone she used


00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.049
in dealing with the bookseller.


00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:43.289
She wanted a rare book
sold only under the counter...


00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.287
- Okay.


00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:45.925
- Which she asked for
with confidence,


00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:51.046
obviously sure that this was
the place to find it.


00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.571
- How much?


00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:56.241
- 100.


00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:57.566
Thank you.


00:19:57.680 --> 00:19:58.966
- Hi.
Remember me?


00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:01.048
- Yes, I remember you.


00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.891
- Hey, wait a minute.


00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.081
Look, no offense.


00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.043
Actually, I didn't mean
anything in particular.


00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:08.366
- What do you want?


00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:09.606
- Nothing.


00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:11.210
Just to talk to you a little.


00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:12.526
- I don't feel like talking.


00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:13.926
I have to bring this back
right away.


00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.451
- To Claire?


